# The image build context is the whole repository root (see Dockerfile's own comment on why: it
# has to COPY this repo's own source to install it locally, per the build workflow's design — see
# .github/workflows/build-image.yaml). Everything below is excluded from what's sent to the
# builder; only pyproject.toml, uv.lock, README.md and obsidian_tools/ are actually COPYed in.
.git/
.github/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.venv/
CHANGELOG.md
CLAUDE.md
DESIGN.md
docs/
tests/
